the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    the dependent child age exemption threshold years is *a number*.
    the care responsibility exemption of *a person* applies.
    *a person* is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements; scenario element.
    *a person* is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of dependent child; scenario element.
    the dependent child age years of *a person* is *a number*; scenario element.
    *a person* is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of incapacitated person; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2015_d_2_b includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(B) — us:statutes/7/2015/d/2/B
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/B.yaml".

rule dependent_child_age_exemption_threshold_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(B)":
the dependent child age exemption threshold years is 6 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule care_responsibility_exemption_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(B)":
the care responsibility exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of dependent child
        and the dependent child age years of the person is a number N
        and the dependent child age exemption threshold years is a number M
        and N < M.

rule care_responsibility_exemption_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(B)":
the care responsibility exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of incapacitated person.

scenario dependent_child_under_age_six_care_responsibility_exempts_person is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/B.test.yaml" at case 1:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the dependent child age years of person_1 is 5.
    person_1 is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of dependent child.
    person_1 is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements.
    q_care_responsibility_exemption_applies expects answers ["the care responsibility exemption of person_1 applies"].

scenario incapacitated_person_care_responsibility_exempts_person is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/B.test.yaml" at case 2:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the dependent child age years of person_1 is 10.
    person_1 is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of incapacitated person.
    person_1 is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements.
    q_care_responsibility_exemption_applies expects answers ["the care responsibility exemption of person_1 applies"].

scenario dependent_child_age_six_or_older_and_no_incapacitated_person_no_exemption is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/B.test.yaml" at case 3:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the dependent child age years of person_1 is 6.
    person_1 is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of dependent child.
    person_1 is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements.
    q_care_responsibility_exemption_applies expects answers [].

scenario person_not_otherwise_required_has_no_exemption_under_this_branch is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/B.test.yaml" at case 4:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the dependent child age years of person_1 is 5.
    person_1 is parent or other household member with responsibility for care of dependent child.
    q_care_responsibility_exemption_applies expects answers [].

query q_care_responsibility_exemption_applies is:
    the care responsibility exemption of which person applies.

